        <briefdescription>
<para>Extract the URI scheme from a location. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This follows Java&apos;s <ref refid="classiceberg_1_1ResolvingFileIO" kindref="compound">ResolvingFileIO</ref>: the text before the first colon is the scheme; an empty result means that no scheme was found. Text that is not syntactically a scheme (RFC 3986) yields no scheme, and on Windows a single letter is a drive rather than a scheme. The rest of the location is not validated. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
